----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 1: PROJECT OVERVIEW & OPERATIONAL OBJECTIVES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.1 Application Objective:
The Paradize Model School (PIS/PMS) Examination & Result Management Suite is a purpose-built,
high-throughput digital ecosystem designed to replace manual tabulation registers, paper mark
sheets, and slow, error-prone spreadsheet entries. It provides:
- Single-portal marks entry for subject teachers with zero lag.
- Centralized administrative broadsheets (Tabulation Registers).
- Automated CBSE/State Board-aligned Report Card generation with instant single and bulk printing.
- Fault-tolerant synchronization with Google Sheets, guaranteeing 100% offline data survivability.

1.2 Target User Personas:
- Subject Teachers: Enter Periodic Tests (PT-1, PT-2, PT-3, PT-4), Half Yearly (HY), and Annual
  Examination (AE) marks, attendance, and qualitative student feedback.
- Class Teachers: Manage class-level student rosters, verify marks, and inspect broadsheets.
- Examination Authority / Admin: Control global entry deadlines, lock/unlock terms, manage subject
  allotments, configure Google Sheets endpoints, and execute official bulk report card print runs.
- Students & Parents: View standardized, tamper-evident printed/digital performance report cards.

1.3 Macro Workflow Lifecycle:
   Admin Allots Subjects & Deadlines -> Teacher Opens App -> Selects Class, Exam & Subject ->
   Enters Marks with Instant Draft & 0.01s Local Sync -> Background Batch Dispatched to Google Sheet ->
   Admin Audits Tabulation Register -> Generates Merits, Broadsheets & Multi-Page Print Report Cards.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 2: TECHNOLOGY STACK & FRAMEWORK INVENTORY
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.1 Client Frontend Core:
- Framework: React 18+ Single Page Application (SPA).
- Language: TypeScript 5.5+ (Strict type enforcement enabled, `--noEmit` passing clean).
- Build Tool: Vite 6.4.3 (ESM production bundler, tree-shaking, fast container startup).
- CSS Framework: Tailwind CSS (v4 compatible, utility-first styling with `@import "tailwindcss"`).
- Icons Library: `lucide-react` (Strict requirement: standard SVG icons, no custom SVG injections).
- Animation & Motion: Native CSS transitions and `@media print` layout engines.

2.2 Backend & Data Ingress Layer:
- Primary Cloud Datastore: Google Sheets (acting as a relational workbook datastore).
- Cloud Middleware: Google Apps Script Web App (GAS) executing JSON-RPC via `doGet` and `doPost`.
- Fallback & Local Database: Browser LocalStorage partitioned by `pis_exam_results_<CLASS>_2025`
  paired with native in-memory caching.
- Runtime Engine: Node.js (Vite development dev server on port 3000, containerized for Cloud Run).

2.3 Core Package Dependencies (`package.json`):
- `react`, `react-dom`: v18+ UI rendering core.
- `lucide-react`: UI icon set for status badges, buttons, and dialogs.
- `clsx`, `tailwind-merge`: Dynamic CSS class resolution (if needed).
- `canvas-confetti` (optional): Merit achievement visual triggers.


