SECTION 14: EXISTING USER EXPERIENCE (UI/UX) & RESPONSIVE DESIGN
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Desktop Precision: Optimized for 1080p and 1440p displays with wide broadsheet tables, side-by-side
  evaluation panels, and instant keyboard shortcuts.
- Mobile Ergonomics: Touch-friendly targets (minimum 44px), sticky student name and roll columns,
  and accessible bottom action drawers.
- Print Formatting: Custom `@media print` rules:
  * Strips headers, footers, navigation buttons, and backgrounds.
  * Sets exact A4 dimensions (210mm x 297mm).
  * Forces page-break isolation between individual student report cards.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 15: RESULT COMPUTATION, TABULATION, GRADING & PDF SYSTEM
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
15.1 CBSE 8-Point Grading Scale:
- 91% to 100% : Grade A1 (Top tier academic distinction)
- 81% to 90%  : Grade A2
- 71% to 80%  : Grade B1
- 61% to 70%  : Grade B2
- 51% to 60%  : Grade C1
- 41% to 50%  : Grade C2
- 33% to 40%  : Grade D  (Pass boundary)
- Below 33%   : Grade E  (Essential Repeat / Remedial required)

15.2 Term Mark Aggregation Formula:
```
PT Converted (Max 10) = (PT1 + PT2) / 4
Internal Total (Max 20) = PT Converted (10) + Portfolio (5) + Subject Enrichment (5)
Subject Total (Max 100) = Internal Total (20) + Written Exam (80)
Dual Exam Grand Total (Max 200) = Half Yearly Total (100) + Annual Exam Total (100)
Grand Percentage (%) = (Grand Total / Maximum Possible Marks) * 100
```

15.3 Result Status Determination:
- PASS: Student secures >= 33% aggregate AND >= 33% in each individual compulsory subject.
- COMPARTMENT: Student fails in up to two subjects with aggregate >= 33%.
- ESSENTIAL REPEAT: Student fails in three or more subjects OR aggregate < 33%.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 16: SECURITY STANDARDS, PRIVACY & DATA HARDENING
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Client-Side Isolation: All data processing, sorting, and grade calculations occur locally.
- Secure Ingress: Google Apps Script Web App endpoints require HTTPS with automated `/exec` redirection.
- No Sensitive Credential Leaks: No hardcoded Google API secrets, service account JSON files, or
  private keys exist in client bundles.
- Anti-Tamper Protection: Admin settings and segment locks require PIN authentication with failed
  attempt lockouts.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 17: CURRENT TECHNICAL BASELINE, KNOWN QUIRKS & SAFE BOUNDARIES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
17.1 Safe Boundaries (What is Working Perfectly):
- Zero-latency 0.01s local mark synchronization between Teacher View and Result Generator.
- Full tabulation broadsheet calculations and merit rank sorting.
- CBSE Report card layout with dual school branding and signature blocks.
- Google Apps Script `/dev` to `/exec` automated diagnostic and correction engine.

17.2 Known Quirks & Workarounds:
- Cross-Domain POST Requests: Browsers dispatching POST requests to Google Apps Script Web Apps
  run under CORS `no-cors` mode. The HTTP response is opaque (status 0). The system assumes
  success upon network completion and verifies data integrity during subsequent GET diagnostic runs.
- Large Photo Base64 Storage: Storing hundreds of high-resolution student photos in LocalStorage can
  approach the 5MB browser quota. It is recommended to keep uploaded photo resolutions under 300KB.


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 18: DEPLOYMENT, APPS SCRIPT RELEASE & ROLLBACK PROCEDURES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
18.1 Google Apps Script Deployment Protocol:
1. Open Google Sheet -> Extensions -> Apps Script.
2. Paste the official Apps Script engine code provided in the handover specification.
3. Click "Deploy" -> "New Deployment".
4. Select Type: "Web App".
5. Set "Execute as": "Me (your Google account)".
6. Set "Who has access": "Anyone" (Required for web client POST access).
7. Copy the resulting URL ending in `/exec` and paste it into App Settings -> PIS Data Base Link.

18.2 Application Production Build:
- Build Command: `npm run build`
- Output Target: `/dist` (Self-contained, production-optimized static assets).
- Deployment Target: Cloud Run / Static CDN hosting.


